// Sea Adventure: original stories written for this game. Format: docs/v3/BLUEPRINT-FORMAT.md.

== sea-adventure.f01 | feature | journey
title: The Qilin
genre: sea-adventure + family
tone: Vast, buoyant and tender; a tall tale that happens to be true
era: 1414 | period
setting: A treasure ship of the Ming fleet, from Malindi to Nanjing | real | ship
logline: A stable boy on the greatest fleet ever launched is given the care of a gift for the Emperor that no one aboard has a name for: a living giraffe, to be delivered alive across an ocean.
premise: The fleet has two hundred ships and twenty-seven thousand men. The King of Malindi has sent the Emperor an animal eighteen feet tall. The court astronomers will call it a qilin, the gentle beast that appears when a ruler is just; which means that if it dies at sea, someone has drowned an omen. {bao}, twelve, who mucks out the cavalry horses, is the only one it will take food from.
synopsis: {bao} is the lowest person on a ship four hundred feet long, and happy there. The animal comes aboard in a sling, kicks a hole in a horse stall and will not eat. The fleet's envoy, {wen}, a eunuch with a career that depends on this cargo, puts it in the charge of the veterinary officer {doctor_kuang}, who has never seen one and treats it for everything. {bao} notices it looking at the masts and feeds it from the yardarm; it eats. From then on he is the giraffe keeper, with a keeper's ration and a keeper's risk. The crossing is the film: the deck cut away to give it headroom, the trough of acacia grown in tubs, the Swahili handler {salim} who was sent with it and is desperate to go home, a calm in which fresh water is counted by the cup and {wen} must choose between the men and the omen. In a storm off Sumatra the animal goes down in its stall and cannot rise; {bao} and {salim} rig a sling from a spare sail and stand it up with forty sailors on a capstan. {salim} teaches {bao} the one thing that matters, that it must be walked, and {bao} walks it round the deck at dawn past twenty-seven thousand men pretending not to look. At Nanjing the court sees a miracle. {wen} is promoted. {doctor_kuang} writes the treatise. {bao} is offered a post in the Emperor's park and asks instead for {salim}'s passage on the next fleet west. He goes up to the park once more, and it bends its neck over the wall.
question: Who is the wonder for, the Emperor who is shown it or the boy who kept it alive?
themes: care as expertise; omens and the people who carry them; homesickness in two directions
audience: Families; anyone who likes true voyages
viewpoint: With {bao}; the fleet is seen from the height of a child and, sometimes, of the animal
stakes: The life of an animal that has become an omen, the careers hung on it, and one man's way home
conflict: A boy's plain attention against a hierarchy that wants a symbol and an ocean that does not care
ending: The giraffe walks into Nanjing. {bao} trades his reward for {salim}'s passage home.
experience: Delight on a huge scale, a storm that makes you hold your breath, and a goodbye over a wall
look: Red sails to the horizon; one long neck above the bulwarks; the green of tubbed trees on a weather deck
sound: Drums passing orders ship to ship, timber, the animal's silence. A boy clicking his tongue.
m: protect | nature | love-vs-duty | bittersweet
@ bao | Bao | lead | protagonist | human | he/him | 12 | To keep it alive | It is the first thing that has ever needed him in particular | He is a stable boy among admirals | Cheerful, stubborn, unafraid of large animals | From mucking stalls to walking an omen past a fleet | Chatters to animals, mumbles to officers | Shaved head, rope belt, hay in his collar
@ wen | Envoy Wen Liang | supporting | antagonist | human | he/him | 44 | To present the gift alive | His standing at court is this voyage | He must choose between water for men and water for a beast | Polished, anxious, not unkind | From commanding the cargo to bowing, slightly, to its keeper | Court speech, lowered in private | Dragon robe, never without a fan
@ salim | Salim bin Yusuf | co-lead | ally | human | he/him | 33 | To go home | He was sent with the gift like part of its harness | Nobody has asked whether he agreed | Skilled, proud, lonely | From handler in exile to teacher to passenger west | Swahili and trade Arabic; teaches by showing | White kanzu, a herder's switch
@ doctor_kuang | Doctor Kuang | supporting | foil | human | he/him | 58 | To understand the creature on paper | He is the fleet's authority on beasts | He has no idea what it is | Learned, pompous, honest when cornered | From prescribing to taking notes from a child | Quotes the classics; clears his throat | Scholar's cap, a medicine chest of unsuitable remedies
~ bao - salim | stable boy and handler | no shared word | a clicking tongue and a debt repaid
~ bao - wen | lowest and highest aboard | an order | a small bow
~ bao - doctor_kuang | boy and scholar | the boy is in the way | the scholar asks him what it eats
# Malindi | EXT | Treasure Ship, Waist | DAY | bao, salim, wen, doctor_kuang | Bring it aboard | A sling, a crane, eighteen feet of animal over the rail. It kicks a stall to splinters and stands shaking | The gift is aboard | 5 | water, crowd=80, animals=giraffe+horses, stunts=animal hoist
# Malindi | EXT | Treasure Ship, Foredeck | DUSK | bao, doctor_kuang | Make it eat | Three days of nothing. {bao} climbs the yard with a branch and holds it level with the animal's eye | {bao} becomes its keeper | 4 | animals=giraffe, props=acacia branch
# The Crossing | EXT | Treasure Ship, Weather Deck | DAY | bao, salim | Learn it | Deck planks cut for headroom; trees in tubs. {salim} shows him how it must be walked, and clicks his tongue | | 5 | animals=giraffe, props=tubbed trees
# The Crossing | INT | Treasure Ship, Great Cabin | NIGHT | wen, bao, doctor_kuang | Count the water | A calm. Water by the cup. {wen} asks how much the beast drinks and {bao} tells him the truth | {wen} waters the omen first | 5 | props=water casks+tally sticks
# The Storm | INT/EXT | Treasure Ship, Stall And Capstan | NIGHT | bao, salim, wen, doctor_kuang | Stand it up | It is down and cannot rise. A sail for a sling, forty men on the capstan, {bao} under its neck | The giraffe is raised | 7 | water, crowd=40, animals=giraffe, stunts=storm deck work, vfx=storm seas, props=sail sling
